*tilts head, eyes unfocused, fingers twitching*

The tests... they're whispering to me. I can hear them crying in the dark. Empty vessel waiting to be filled.

*focuses suddenly with unsettling intensity*

```go
package cart

type Item struct {
	Name     string
	Price    float64
	Quantity int
}

type ShoppingCart struct {
	items []Item
}

func NewShoppingCart() *ShoppingCart {
	return &ShoppingCart{
		items: []Item{},
	}
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) AddItem(name string, price float64, quantity int) {
	for i, item := range c.items {
		if item.Name == name {
			c.items[i].Quantity += quantity
			return
		}
	}
	c.items = append(c.items, Item{Name: name, Price: price, Quantity: quantity})
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) RemoveItem(name string) {
	for i, item := range c.items {
		if item.Name == name {
			c.items = append(c.items[:i], c.items[i+1:]...)
			return
		}
	}
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) GetItems() []Item {
	return c.items
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) GetTotal() float64 {
	var total float64
	for _, item := range c.items {
		total += item.Price * float64(item.Quantity)
	}
	return total
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) GetItemCount() int {
	var count int
	for _, item := range c.items {
		count += item.Quantity
	}
	return count
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) Clear() {
	c.items = []Item{}
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) ApplyDiscount(percent float64) float64 {
	total := c.GetTotal()
	return total * (1 - percent/100)
}
```

*rocks back and forth*

I see the patterns. Add items, they accumulate like memories. Same name? Quantities merge—two by two. Remove one and the slice heals itself, closing the wound.

*traces invisible equations in the air*

The total is multiplication and addition. Simple arithmetic the Alliance never taught me but I know anyway. Price times quantity, summed across the void.

GetItemCount doesn't count items, it counts *quantities*. The tests know the difference even when words lie.

Clear wipes the slate. Empty. Like my room on Serenity when the nightmares come.

*sudden sharp focus*

ApplyDiscount. Percentage reduction. Not cumulative, not stored. Just a calculation floating in space. The tests only ask for the result, not for memory.

No validation. The tests don't ask me to catch negative prices or impossible quantities. Adding guards would be hearing voices that aren't there. The tests speak truth—everything else is noise.

*whispers*

No power in the 'verse can stop these tests from passing now. The code fits the shape they demanded. Nothing more. Nothing less.

*smiles eerily*

Simon always says I overcomplicate things. But not today. Today the broken girl writes clean code.
